	(text "SCHEMATIC REVIEW / RELEASE HOLDS\n1. U1 uses A1-A19 / J1-J19 from SigilBackMarked.png (BACK view); never exchange row identities.\n2. No DevKit footprint assigned: measure pitch, row spacing, outline, USB-C overhang, holes, socket height and keepouts.\n3. Future footprint: two 1x19 female sockets, unmistakable A1/J1 marks; verify insertion from carrier component side.\n4. Keep USB-C, BOOT and EN/reset accessible; preserve antenna/component clearances after measurement.\n5. Display/joystick/d-pad/ring headers and R1 have no footprint and the buzzer is a logical interface; all are excluded from PCB and BOM.\n6. Discrete LEDs and the old buttons are removed; J4 is the five-button d-pad (switches to GND); J5 is the NeoPixel status ring on USB 5V.\n7. Rev A is an electrical draft, NOT fabrication-ready. Power through DevKit USB; no second supply designed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28 211 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3853969e-2f08-52c0-8854-2e912f1f8895")
	)
	(text "Five momentary switches, each from its key to GND; the ESP32\ninternal pull-ups need no resistors. Up/Down move the menu\nlist, Select or Right choose, Left closes. Pair is the DevKit\nBOOT button. Firmware: Sigil PlatformIO env sigil-oled."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290 91.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "654ecefd-70be-5287-813e-7936edb002dc")
	)
	(text "BACK / REAR PHOTO VIEW\nJ1 (5V) top-left; A1 (CLK) top-right\nSocket IDs are immutable; this is NOT a footprint view."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28 21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "694c6bf1-7687-5c82-ac3e-49dde90b17d9")
	)
	(text "DISPLAY"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175 40 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "918b9a6a-a89e-5b4a-ba65-5ba264b74363")
	)
	(text "Adafruit NeoPixel Jewel 7, RGBW, powered from USB 5V (J1).\n3.3 V data into 5 V pixels usually works; if it glitches, add a\n74AHCT125 level shifter. R1 (300-500 ohm) sits at the ring.\nRecommended, not fitted on the breadboard: 100-1000 uF across\nPWR/GND. Full RGBW is ~80 mA per pixel (~560 mA total), more\nthan USB supplies: firmware caps brightness at 48/255.\nDraws the status light (LedState); never the only signal.\nFirmware: Sigil PlatformIO env sigil or sigil-oled."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a6a5ecb7-15ea-5f9b-ade9-03568efa8075")
	)
	(text "Wire colours are the breadboard jumpers in the owner photos\n(2026-09-24), not a harness specification.\nInland 1.3\" OLED V2.0 (KS0056), 4-wire SPI, 3.3 V.\nSH1106 128x64 inferred from the vendor example.\nJ2 pins follow the board header, pin 1 = GND (top).\nGPIO21 (A14, the e-ink BUSY) is Right on the d-pad here."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175 96.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a982025d-593d-5024-b4a1-e534a015a663")
	)
	(text "gray wire"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 204.47 69.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ba739cdf-03b9-5442-a037-4c32ed04cc45")
	)
	(text "J3 is an unresolved load interface.\nConfirm transducer/driver, current and protection.\nNo direct-drive suitability is assumed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175 162 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bd67c9ee-5518-5916-b933-2caada413c12")
	)
	(text "blue wire"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 204.47 79.76 0)
		(effects
